# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# mcp-news environment
#
# YOU DO NOT NEED THIS FILE. `docker compose up` starts without it, and the
# setup wizard in your browser configures everything on the happy path.
#
# It exists for two things only:
#   1. API keys, which are deliberately never written into a configuration file.
#   2. Overriding where the application looks for its files, which is normally
#      the container's job rather than yours.
#
# With nothing set, the application runs at level 0: it collects, de-duplicates,
# archives, keyword-searches and ranks against your interests. Add a provider
# later and `mcpnews enrich --backlog` processes what you already collected.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Keys for AI models, if you configure any ------------------------------
# Point the slots at an endpoint in Settings -> AI models. That screen stores the
# *name* of the variable holding each key; the key itself only ever lives here.

# Local / private engines. Any OpenAI-compatible server: llama.cpp, Ollama,
# LM Studio, vLLM, TEI. Most need no key at all.
LOCAL_CHAT_API_KEY=
LOCAL_EMBED_API_KEY=

# Cloud engines. Until the matching key is set, these slots count as
# unconfigured and the application will not claim a capability level it cannot
# deliver.
CLOUD_CHAT_API_KEY=
CLOUD_EMBED_API_KEY=

# --- Overrides you will rarely want ----------------------------------------
# The wizard offers these as defaults and stores whatever you choose in
# config/settings.yaml, which then takes precedence over anything set here.
# MCPNEWS_CONFIG_DIR=/app/config
# MCPNEWS_DATA_DIR=/data
# MCPNEWS_ARCHIVE_DIR=/archive

# Host port for the dashboard. Bound to 127.0.0.1 by docker-compose.yml.
# MCPNEWS_PORT=8378

# MCPNEWS_LOG_LEVEL=INFO
